  message: "iter-002 validation (deep-20260621-215349/cohort-002/iter-002, post PR #4263): WI-rijup claim VALIDATED MOVED -- pretix rst/vue/scss nonconforming stable_id 1223->0, chatwoot vue/scss 12664->0. Moved for the RIGHT reason: node counts byte-identical (pretix 31095->31095, chatwoot 44372->44372; doc-node counts rst 821/vue 284/scss 118 and vue 14387/scss 3 unchanged), node.id byte-identical iter1<->iter2 (0 added/removed), 0 new stable_id collisions. No regression on the other cohort claims (ts_extends 86, inherited 11455/16, refs->pyvar 922, bare_hex 0). awaits_bakeoff_validation tag STRIPPED (the shipped WI-rijup claim is validated moved). BUT INV-hunup is NOT satisfied -> status remains violated: iter-002 surfaced a residual the cohort+grep had missed, and a codebase-wide scope-expansion found MORE non-canonical stable_id producers beyond WI-rijup's 9 doc analyzers: (1) graphql-linker linkers/graphql.py:223 stable_id=call.operation_name on synthetic graphql_client nodes (language=None) -- surfaced live on apollo-server as stable_id='test' from 'query test{...}'; (2) sparql.py (3 sites) stable_id=symbol_id -- EXACT WI-rijup antipattern, MISSED by WI-rijup's grep; (3) kdl.py stable_id=symbol_id -- same, MISSED; (4) scip/index.py:203 stable_id=sym_info.symbol (SCIP moniker) -- needs judgment (hash-to-canonical vs document-exempt). wgsl.py:234 verified canonical (make_entry_stable_id/None). Remediation to be filed; WI-rijup's 'found exactly these 9 producers' claim was incomplete (grep blind spot: only matched analyzers with =symbol_id and was not run over linkers/scip)."  # d907
